What was wrong:  
The PR initially contained a faulty test and insufficient test coverage. The CI run identified the test issue and showed that coverage was below the required threshold.

Why CI caught it:  
The test workflow automatically ran the test suite on the pull request, while the coverage workflow measured coverage and failed when it was below 85%. This allowed the problems to be detected automatically before the changes were merged
